doc:sec-9d-ss-1b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9D(1B) Variation of entries in Register" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1B) If: (a) a medicine is included in the part of the Register for goods known as provisionally registered goods; and (b) the Secretary makes a decision under subsection 29(9) to extend the provisional registration period for the medicine; the Secretary may, on the Secretary’s own initiative, vary the entry in the Register in relation to the medicine to reduce the class of persons for whom the medicine is suitable or to change the directions for use. Note: The Secretary may also vary the product information relating to the medicine: see subsection 25AA(4)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-1c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9D(1C) Variation of entries in Register"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-9d-ss-1c ;
    values:originalText "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A) or (1B), the Secretary must: (a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered written notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for the proposed variation; and (b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a submission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed variation; and  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with paragraph (b)—take the submission into account before making a decision whether or not to make the variation." ;
    skos:definition "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A) or (1B), the Secretary must: (a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered written notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for the proposed variation; and (b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a submission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed variation; and  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with paragraph (b)—take the submission into account before making a decision whether or not to make the variation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "85142cccf63885ba5352f3f582139f32a1a19c4606a818191d4c8252a6a97801" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Secretary must give notice and opportunity to submit before making variation." ;
    dc:description "written notice, submission" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
