    values:originalText "(1C) If the Secretary proposes to make a variation under subsection (1A) or (1B), the Secretary must: (a) give the person in relation to whom the medicine is registered written notice of the proposed variation and of the reasons for the proposed variation; and (b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make a submission to the Secretary in relation to the proposed variation; and  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Chapter 2  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) if the person makes a submission in accordance with paragraph (b)—take the submission into account before making a decision whether or not to make the variation." ;
