concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9D(3) Variation of entries in Register"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-9d-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) the person in relation to whom therapeutic goods are registered or listed has requested the Secretary to vary  Chapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the goods; and (b) subsection (2) does not apply to the request; and (ba) subsection (2C) does not apply to the request; and (c) the Secretary is satisfied that the variation requested does not indicate any reduction in the quality, safety or efficacy of the goods for the purposes for which they are to be used; the Secretary may vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3AA) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a biological is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the biological; and (b) the only effect of the variation would be: (i) to reduce the class of persons for whom the biological is suitable; or (ii) to add a warning, or precaution, that does not include any comparison of the biological with any other therapeutic goods by reference to quality, safety or efficacy; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3AC) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a biological is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary the entry in the Register that relates to the biological; and (b) the variation is of a kind specified in the regulations; and (c) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If: (a) the person in relation to whom therapeutic goods are registered or listed has requested the Secretary to vary  Chapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the goods; and (b) subsection (2) does not apply to the request; and (ba) subsection (2C) does not apply to the request; and (c) the Secretary is satisfied that the variation requested does not indicate any reduction in the quality, safety or efficacy of the goods for the purposes for which they are to be used; the Secretary may vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3AA) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a biological is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the biological; and (b) the only effect of the variation would be: (i) to reduce the class of persons for whom the biological is suitable; or (ii) to add a warning, or precaution, that does not include any comparison of the biological with any other therapeutic goods by reference to quality, safety or efficacy; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3AC) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a biological is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary the entry in the Register that relates to the biological; and (b) the variation is of a kind specified in the regulations; and (c) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b32b31452e17103c8ea14d4dfa410bf0bd23e58c8a1dc2ba799d6a91b98c5c52" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Secretary may vary entry in Register upon request." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
