doc:sec-9d-ss-3b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9D(3B) Variation of entries in Register" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3B) If: (a) a particular biological ceases to be a biological because of a determination under subsection 32A(3); and (b) the biological is included in the Register under Part 3-2A; the Secretary must move the entry relating to the biological from the part of the Register for biologicals to whichever other part of the Register is applicable." ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d-ss-3c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9D(3C) Variation of entries in Register"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-9d-ss-3c ;
    values:originalText "(3C) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the kind of medical device; and (b) the only effect of the variation would be: (i) to reduce the class of persons for whom the kind of medical device is suitable; or (ii) to add a warning, restriction or precaution, that does not include any comparison of the kind of medical device with any other therapeutic goods by reference to quality, safety or performance; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3CB) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary the entry in the Register that relates to the kind of medical device; and (b) the variation is of a kind specified in the regulations; and  Chapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request." ;
    skos:definition "(3C) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary information included in the entry in the Register that relates to the kind of medical device; and (b) the only effect of the variation would be: (i) to reduce the class of persons for whom the kind of medical device is suitable; or (ii) to add a warning, restriction or precaution, that does not include any comparison of the kind of medical device with any other therapeutic goods by reference to quality, safety or performance; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request. (3CB) If: (a) the person in relation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register has requested the Secretary to vary the entry in the Register that relates to the kind of medical device; and (b) the variation is of a kind specified in the regulations; and  Chapter 2  Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods  Section 9D Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; the Secretary must vary the entry in accordance with the request."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0200ff3c57bdf9899fdff339cf2574e201d8017db0935fda2cb585532d4ad480" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-9d ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
