    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14-ss-4a ;
    values:originalText "(4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and (b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the Secretary; and (c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the goods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling or packaging). Penalty: 100 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person imports therapeutic goods into Australia; and (b) the goods are imported without the consent in writing of the Secretary; and (c) the goods do not conform with a standard applicable to the goods (other than by reason of a matter relating to labelling or packaging). Penalty: 100 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "24deb619fdf5af99d5c530f55e1fbd2ebff255142980fd67d944b62cc3be666d" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-14 ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Importing therapeutic goods without consent is prohibited." ;
