concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Therapeutic goods and gazetted groups"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, therapeutic goods (other than medicine of the kind to which subsection (1A) applies) are to be taken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if they have: (a) a different formulation, composition or design specification; or (b) a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or (c) a different dosage form or model; or (d) a different name; or  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, therapeutic goods (other than medicine of the kind to which subsection (1A) applies) are to be taken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if they have: (a) a different formulation, composition or design specification; or (b) a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or (c) a different dosage form or model; or (d) a different name; or  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "332e821bf3e340d296550535e75847a6b2321f16e76111ab1ed0f75d5815c2bb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "89"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Therapeutic goods must be taken to be separate and distinct from other therapeutic goods if they have a different formulation, composition or design specification; or a different strength or size (disregarding pack size); or a different dosage form or model; or a different name;" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.89" ;
