doc:sec-19-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19(3) Approvals or authorities for certain uses" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting the conditions to which an approval under subsection (1) may be made subject, those conditions may include a condition relating to the charges that may be made for the therapeutic goods to which the approval relates." ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19(4) Approvals or authorities for certain uses"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-19-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Where an application for an approval is made, the Secretary must, after having considered the application and, in the case of an application for the use of therapeutic goods for experimental purposes in humans, after having evaluated the information submitted with the application, notify the applicant of the decision on the application within 28 days of making the decision and, in the case of a decision not to grant the approval, of the reasons for the decision." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Where an application for an approval is made, the Secretary must, after having considered the application and, in the case of an application for the use of therapeutic goods for experimental purposes in humans, after having evaluated the information submitted with the application, notify the applicant of the decision on the application within 28 days of making the decision and, in the case of a decision not to grant the approval, of the reasons for the decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2444276c81866ecd86b77a89a253735c272a7de395f037589e5c55cbc5e0431a" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19 ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notify applicant of decision on approval within 28 days." ;
    dc:description "Reasons for decision (if not granting approval)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
