concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-19c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19C Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-19c ;
    values:originalText "under subsection 19B(6) (1) If: (a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against subsection 19B(1); or (b) an offence against subsection 19B(1) is to be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; the committing magistrate or the court must: (c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and (d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant. (2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence in support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless: (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the trial begins; or (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the hearing of the offence begins; he or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "under subsection 19B(6) (1) If: (a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against subsection 19B(1); or (b) an offence against subsection 19B(1) is to be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; the committing magistrate or the court must: (c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and (d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant. (2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence in support of the exception under subsection 19B(6) unless: (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the trial begins; or (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the hearing of the offence begins; he or she gives notice of particulars of the exception.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77146b6ede20dfed3c542c124cb75182179bf06dcb289624c7d97eac832e7e37" ;
    cof:pageNumber "109"^^xsd:integer ;
