concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22F Revocation of provisional determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-22f ;
    values:originalText "Revocation on Secretary’s own initiative (1) The Secretary may revoke a provisional determination under section 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the Secretary is satisfied that the criteria prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of subsection 22D(2) are no longer met in relation to the medicine. Revocation on request (2) The Secretary must revoke a provisional determination under section 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the person requests the Secretary, in writing, to do so. Notice of revocation (3) As soon as practicable after making a revocation under this section, the Secretary must: (a) give the person written notice of the revocation; and (b) for a revocation under subsection (1)—set out the reasons for the revocation in the notice.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Provisional determinations for medicine  Division 1A Section 22F Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Day revocation takes effect (4) A revocation under this section takes effect on the day on which the Secretary gives the person notice of the revocation.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "Revocation on Secretary’s own initiative (1) The Secretary may revoke a provisional determination under section 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the Secretary is satisfied that the criteria prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of subsection 22D(2) are no longer met in relation to the medicine. Revocation on request (2) The Secretary must revoke a provisional determination under section 22D relating to a person and a medicine if the person requests the Secretary, in writing, to do so. Notice of revocation (3) As soon as practicable after making a revocation under this section, the Secretary must: (a) give the person written notice of the revocation; and (b) for a revocation under subsection (1)—set out the reasons for the revocation in the notice.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Provisional determinations for medicine  Division 1A Section 22F Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Day revocation takes effect (4) A revocation under this section takes effect on the day on which the Secretary gives the person notice of the revocation.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6e75ab479905bdbba7c1e57d0311cfe9c0adf3a3549977464ca792bb1bc13261" ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-22f-ss-2 ;
