doc:sec-23b-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23B(2) Requirements relating to applications for registration of" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The requirements are as follows: (a) the application must be made: (i) in accordance with the form approved, in writing, by the Secretary for that class of therapeutic goods; or (ii) in such other manner as is approved, in writing, by the Secretary for that class of therapeutic goods;  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "141"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23C Requirements relating to applications for listing of therapeutic"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23c ;
    values:originalText "goods under section 26 or 26A (1) This section applies if an application is made under section 23 for listing of therapeutic goods under section 26 or 26A. (2) The application complies with this section if: (a) the application is made in accordance with a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary or in such other manner as is approved, in writing, by the Secretary for the purposes of this paragraph; and (b) the application is delivered to an office of the Department specified by the Secretary; and (c) the prescribed application fee has been paid; and (d) the applicant has delivered to the office to which the application was made such information, in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary, as will allow the determination of the application; and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 23C Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (e) if the Secretary so requires—the applicant has delivered to the office to which the application was made a reasonable number of samples of the goods; and (f) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the purposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the application is accompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying that: (i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (g) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—the application is accompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying that: (i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those conditions; and (ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those conditions; and (iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those conditions. Note: To be listed, an application must comply with this section: see sections 26, 26A and 26AB. (3) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, determine forms of information for the purposes of the application of paragraph (2)(d).  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "goods under section 26 or 26A (1) This section applies if an application is made under section 23 for listing of therapeutic goods under section 26 or 26A. (2) The application complies with this section if: (a) the application is made in accordance with a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary or in such other manner as is approved, in writing, by the Secretary for the purposes of this paragraph; and (b) the application is delivered to an office of the Department specified by the Secretary; and (c) the prescribed application fee has been paid; and (d) the applicant has delivered to the office to which the application was made such information, in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary, as will allow the determination of the application; and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 23C Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (e) if the Secretary so requires—the applicant has delivered to the office to which the application was made a reasonable number of samples of the goods; and (f) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the purposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the application is accompanied by a statement from the applicant certifying that: (i) if those prohibitions cover imports—any imports into Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (ii) if those prohibitions cover exports—any exports from Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (iii) if those prohibitions cover supplies—any supplies in Australia of the goods by, or on behalf of the applicant, will not contravene those prohibitions; and (g) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—the application is accompanied by a statement f"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6cbcba44011f176dc0c6a57bda4e764b1df7b821038bfa37bbba63d9e1603dd9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "144"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-23c-ss-3 ;
