concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24E Deemed refusal of application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24e ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies in the case of an application under section 23 in relation to therapeutic goods for the evaluation of which a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(da). (2) If, at the end of the period referred to in subsection (1), the evaluation has not been completed, the applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused. (3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the evaluation is completed. (4) Where a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has effect as if: (a) the Secretary had decided not to register the goods the subject of the application; and (b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3) confirming the decision of the Secretary; and (c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which notice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2).  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 25 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies in the case of an application under section 23 in relation to therapeutic goods for the evaluation of which a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(da). (2) If, at the end of the period referred to in subsection (1), the evaluation has not been completed, the applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused. (3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the evaluation is completed. (4) Where a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has effect as if: (a) the Secretary had decided not to register the goods the subject of the application; and (b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3) confirming the decision of the Secretary; and (c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which notice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2).  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 25 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b91ca0625e5fd5ee14a17be0d1e098e53992384c9eb938e6a42662aa913acfd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24e-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24e-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24e-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-24e-ss-4 ;
