concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26AD Lapsing and deemed refusal of applications for listing of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-26ad ;
    values:originalText "medicine under section 26AE Lapsing of applications (1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE lapses if: (a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC remains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which the amount became due and payable; or (b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular; or (c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the applicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular. Deemed refusal of applications (2) If: (a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa) prescribe a period within which evaluations under section 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed; and (b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been completed; the applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused. (3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the evaluation is completed.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 26AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has effect as if: (a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is the subject of the application; and (b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3) confirming the decision of the Secretary; and (c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which notice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2)." ;
    skos:definition "medicine under section 26AE Lapsing of applications (1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE lapses if: (a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC remains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which the amount became due and payable; or (b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular; or (c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the applicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular. Deemed refusal of applications (2) If: (a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa) prescribe a period within which evaluations under section 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed; and (b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been completed; the applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused. (3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the evaluation is completed.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 26AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has effect as if: (a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is the subject of the application; and (b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3) confirming the decision of the Secretary; and (c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which notice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "68f39f5b384d9e42a9e3cb3607877a04c5a02447c47a83d8f1956cb38f3ba234" ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26ad-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.174" .
doc:sec-26ad a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26AD Lapsing and deemed refusal of applications for listing of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "medicine under section 26AE Lapsing of applications (1) An application for the listing of a medicine under section 26AE lapses if: (a) any part of the evaluation fee referred to in section 26AC remains unpaid at the end of 28 days after the day on which the amount became due and payable; or (b) the application contains information that is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular; or (c) information given to the Secretary by, or on behalf of, the applicant in connection with the application is inaccurate or misleading in a material particular. Deemed refusal of applications (2) If: (a) regulations made for the purposes of paragraph 63(2)(daaaa) prescribe a period within which evaluations under section 26AE in relation to the medicine must be completed; and (b) at the end of that period, the evaluation has not been completed; the applicant may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused. (3) A notice under subsection (2) may be given at any time before the evaluation is completed.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 26AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (4) If a notice has been given, this Act (except subsection 60(5)) has effect as if: (a) the Secretary had decided not to list the medicine which is the subject of the application; and (b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3) confirming the decision of the Secretary; and (c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which notice was given to the Secretary under subsection (2)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer .

