concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26BF Permissible indications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-26bf ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination in relation to either or both of the following: (a) indications; (b) requirements in relation to indications. Note: See paragraphs 26A(2)(fba), (fd) and (fe) (which deal with matters that a person seeking the listing of a medicine under section 26A must certify). (2) In deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1) in relation to a particular indication, the Minister may have regard to whether the indication is a therapeutic use that relates to one or more of the following: (a) maintaining health; (b) enhancing health; (c) preventing a dietary deficiency;  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 26BG Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (d) a disease, ailment, defect or injury, other than a serious form of the disease, ailment, defect or injury. (3) Subsection (2) does not limit the matters to which the Minister may have regard in deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1) in relation to a particular indication. (4) Without limiting paragraph (1)(b), the requirements may relate to: (a) the use of particular indications in specified circumstances; or (b) the use of particular indications if certain specified conditions are met. (5) A determination under paragraph (1)(b) may make different provision for different classes of medicines. (6) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a determination under subsection (1) of this section may make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination in relation to either or both of the following: (a) indications; (b) requirements in relation to indications. Note: See paragraphs 26A(2)(fba), (fd) and (fe) (which deal with matters that a person seeking the listing of a medicine under section 26A must certify). (2) In deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1) in relation to a particular indication, the Minister may have regard to whether the indication is a therapeutic use that relates to one or more of the following: (a) maintaining health; (b) enhancing health; (c) preventing a dietary deficiency;  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 Registration and listing  Division 2 Section 26BG Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (d) a disease, ailment, defect or injury, other than a serious form of the disease, ailment, defect or injury. (3) Subsection (2) does not limit the matters to which the Minister may have regard in deciding whether to make a determination under subsection (1) in relation to a particular indication. (4) Without limiting paragraph (1)(b), the requirements may relate to: (a) the use of particular indications in specified circumstances; or (b) the use of particular indications if certain specified conditions are met. (5) A determination under paragraph (1)(b) may make different provision for different classes of medicines. (6) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a determination under subsection (1) of this section may make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c29e1efc49a0f59edffe8e0093141ff501d6dfc7e7f47f62a53765e84f8b4984" ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26bf-ss-4 ;
