concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26D Requirements for interlocutory injunction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-26d ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies where: (a) an applicant gives notice to a patentee in accordance with subparagraph 26B(1)(b)(iii); and (b) the patentee and/or its exclusive licensee (in this section the party or parties is or are referred to as the patentee) applies to a prescribed court for an interlocutory injunction to restrain the applicant from marketing the therapeutic goods the subject of the application on the ground that such conduct will constitute an infringement of its patent. (2) An application for interlocutory relief in accordance with subsection (1) may not be instituted unless the patentee has first notified the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth, or of a State or of a Territory, in writing of the application.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies where: (a) an applicant gives notice to a patentee in accordance with subparagraph 26B(1)(b)(iii); and (b) the patentee and/or its exclusive licensee (in this section the party or parties is or are referred to as the patentee) applies to a prescribed court for an interlocutory injunction to restrain the applicant from marketing the therapeutic goods the subject of the application on the ground that such conduct will constitute an infringement of its patent. (2) An application for interlocutory relief in accordance with subsection (1) may not be instituted unless the patentee has first notified the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth, or of a State or of a Territory, in writing of the application.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "70f2b748e70d28ac0ab6dbb7661181038f8a664b8b8092c1c90b43c1aa7f9242" ;
    cof:pageNumber "193"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-26d-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.193" .
