concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-30g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30G Disposal of unused goods exempt under section 18A"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-30g ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to particular therapeutic goods if: (a) an exemption in relation to those goods under section 18A ceases to have effect otherwise than because those goods have become registered goods or listed goods (see paragraph 18A(5)(a)); and (b) those goods have not been used before the exemption so ceases to have effect.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 General  Division 3 Section 30H Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of any of those goods in accordance with the regulations. (3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out the methods by which those goods are to be stored, supplied, destroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of. (4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not enable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including the Commonwealth) other than the owner of those goods." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to particular therapeutic goods if: (a) an exemption in relation to those goods under section 18A ceases to have effect otherwise than because those goods have become registered goods or listed goods (see paragraph 18A(5)(a)); and (b) those goods have not been used before the exemption so ceases to have effect.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Registration and listing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-2 General  Division 3 Section 30H Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of any of those goods in accordance with the regulations. (3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out the methods by which those goods are to be stored, supplied, destroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of. (4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not enable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including the Commonwealth) other than the owner of those goods."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45ff15ef881a4e851ca91e68bc2e683c331cdfd2cc5574bdf871b67018649bf7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "240"^^xsd:integer ;
