concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32AA Biological classes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32aa ;
    values:originalText "The regulations may prescribe different classes of biologicals. Note 1: The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological included in a class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other biologicals: see section 32AB. Note 2: The Secretary may approve different application forms for different classes of biologicals: see section 32DDA. 32AB  When biologicals are separate and distinct from other biologicals (1) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological included in a specified class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other biologicals. (2) The regulations may make different provision in relation to different classes of biologicals that are prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of section 32AA.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Preliminary  Division 1 Section 32AB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Note: The Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register if the biological has changed so that it has become separate and distinct from the biological as so included: see subsection 32GC(1).  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "The regulations may prescribe different classes of biologicals. Note 1: The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological included in a class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other biologicals: see section 32AB. Note 2: The Secretary may approve different application forms for different classes of biologicals: see section 32DDA. 32AB  When biologicals are separate and distinct from other biologicals (1) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which a biological included in a specified class of biologicals is separate and distinct from other biologicals. (2) The regulations may make different provision in relation to different classes of biologicals that are prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of section 32AA.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Preliminary  Division 1 Section 32AB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Note: The Secretary may cancel the entry of a biological from the Register if the biological has changed so that it has become separate and distinct from the biological as so included: see subsection 32GC(1).  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5351deba72f85072074e55b47a197b99059c1f3308d53b3d552e7a0124d0bc6c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "260"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32aa-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.260" .
