doc:sec-32bd-ss-4a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32BD(4A) Criminal offences for supplying a biological" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person supplies in Australia a biological for use in humans; and (b) none of the following subparagraphs applies: (i) the biological is included in the Register in relation to the person; (ii) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in relation to the biological or the biological is exempt under subsection 32CA(2);  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "270"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32be a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32BE Notice required to adduce evidence in support of exception to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32be ;
    values:originalText "offences (1) If: (a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against subsection 32BA(1), 32BB(1), 32BC(1) or 32BD(1); or (b) an offence against subsection 32BA(1), 32BB(1), 32BC(1) or 32BD(1) is to be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; the committing magistrate or the court must: (c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and (d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant. (2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence in support of the exception under subsection 32BA(6), 32BB(6), 32BC(6) or 32BD(6) unless the defendant gives notice of particulars of the exception: (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the trial begins; or (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the hearing of the offence begins. (3) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, call any other person to give evidence in support of the exception unless: (a) the notice under subsection (2) includes the name and address of the person or, if the name and address is not known to the defendant at the time the defendant gives the notice, any information in the defendant’s possession that might be of material assistance in finding the person; and (b) if the name or the address is not included in the notice—the court is satisfied that the defendant before giving the notice took, and after giving the notice continued to take, all reasonable steps to ascertain the name or address; and  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "offences (1) If: (a) a defendant is committed for trial for an offence against subsection 32BA(1), 32BB(1), 32BC(1) or 32BD(1); or (b) an offence against subsection 32BA(1), 32BB(1), 32BC(1) or 32BD(1) is to be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; the committing magistrate or the court must: (c) inform the defendant of the requirements of this section; and (d) cause a copy of this section to be given to the defendant. (2) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, adduce evidence in support of the exception under subsection 32BA(6), 32BB(6), 32BC(6) or 32BD(6) unless the defendant gives notice of particulars of the exception: (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies—more than 21 days before the trial begins; or (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—more than 21 days before the hearing of the offence begins. (3) A defendant must not, without leave of the court, call any other person to give evidence in support of the exception unless: (a) the notice under subsection (2) includes the name and address of the person or, if the name and address is not known to the defendant at the time the defendant gives the notice, any information in the defendant’s possession that might be of material assistance in finding the person; and (b) if the name or the address is not included in the notice—the court is satisfied that the defendant before giving the notice took, and after giving the notice continued to take, all reasonable steps to ascertain the name or address; and  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3b1136af07e5f03743ec4abe274eef1fe23ae5890e24a975247fc98d3bba8c9d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "273"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32be-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32be-ss-2 ;
