doc:sec-32c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32C What this Division is about" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "There are 4 kinds of exemptions in relation to biologicals: (a) exemptions of biologicals under the regulations; and (b) exemptions of biologicals to deal with emergencies; and (c) exemptions of biologicals for special and experimental uses; and (d) exemptions of biologicals where substitutes are unavailable. Subdivision B—Exempting biologicals under the regulations" ;
    cof:pageNumber "288"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32CA Exempt biologicals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32ca ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulations may exempt specified persons from the operation of Division 4 in relation to specified biologicals. Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003. (2) The regulations may exempt specified biologicals from the operation of Division 4. Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003. (3) An exemption under this section may be subject to conditions that are prescribed in the regulations. Note: There are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of a condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ. (5) If the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes effect on the day specified in the regulations. The day must not be earlier  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 than 28 days after the day on which the regulations revoking the exemption take effect. Subdivision C—Exempting biologicals to deal with emergencies" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulations may exempt specified persons from the operation of Division 4 in relation to specified biologicals. Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003. (2) The regulations may exempt specified biologicals from the operation of Division 4. Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003. (3) An exemption under this section may be subject to conditions that are prescribed in the regulations. Note: There are criminal offences and a civil penalty related to the breach of a condition of an exemption: see sections 32CP and 32CQ. (5) If the regulations revoke an exemption, the revocation takes effect on the day specified in the regulations. The day must not be earlier  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 than 28 days after the day on which the regulations revoking the exemption take effect. Subdivision C—Exempting biologicals to deal with emergencies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "db82edd594c1204b50881db698f8ea10f8b6ff23fcb840bb2fcc00072c71b7b6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "288"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ca-ss-5 ;
