doc:sec-32cj-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32CJ(6) Criminal offences and civil penalty for biologicals not" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under subsection (2); and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CJ Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in subsection (3); and (c) the person fails to comply with that requirement; and (d) either: (i) the use of any of the biologicals has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of any of the biologicals, if any of the biologicals were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and (e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result, would result, or would be likely to result, because the person failed to comply with that requirement. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA." ;
    cof:pageNumber "294"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32CJ(7) Criminal offences and civil penalty for biologicals not"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32cj-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under subsection (2); and (b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in subsection (3); and (c) the person fails to comply with that requirement. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both." ;
    skos:definition "(7) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary gives a notice to the person under subsection (2); and (b) the notice specifies a particular requirement mentioned in subsection (3); and (c) the person fails to comply with that requirement. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d97606b3646e0c55b11f306658674f3ce38bb019beaa2267212f86b749c46fc1" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cj ;
    cof:pageNumber "294"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with notice requirement is an offence." ;
