concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cn a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32CN Criminal offences relating to the giving of an authority to a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32cn ;
    values:originalText "health practitioner (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CN Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6); and (d) either: (i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and (e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result, would result, or would be likely to result, because: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; or (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. (4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: 500 penalty units. (4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies:  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "health practitioner (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CN Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6); and (d) either: (i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and (e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result, would result, or would be likely to result, because: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; or (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. (4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: 500 penalty units. (4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies:  Chap"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "73c01c8f80eb06d9ed352e080ae678a2a850abaa2b279eb92f5cd3e14cbf2fa5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "302"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cn-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cn-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32cn-ss-4a ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.302" .
doc:sec-32cn a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32CN Criminal offences relating to the giving of an authority to a" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "health practitioner (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Exemptions  Division 3 Section 32CN Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6); and (d) either: (i) the use of the biological has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the biological, if the biological were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; and (e) the harm or injury has resulted, will result, is likely to result, would result, or would be likely to result, because: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; or (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. (4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: 500 penalty units. (4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies:  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "302"^^xsd:integer .

