    values:originalText "(4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: 500 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the Secretary has authorised, under subsection 32CM(1), the person to supply a biological; and (b) the person supplies the biological; and (c) either of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with the authority; (iii) the supply is not in accordance with regulations made for the purpose of subsection 32CM(6). Penalty: 500 penalty units."@en ;
