doc:sec-32h a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32H What this Division is about" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Secretary may require a person to recall biologicals, or to inform the public about biologicals, that do not comply with requirements or cannot lawfully be supplied. There are criminal offences and a civil penalty for breaching such a requirement." ;
    cof:pageNumber "360"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-32ha a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32HA Public notification, and recall, of biologicals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32ha ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, impose requirements, relating to a biological, on a person if: (a) any of the circumstances referred to in the 2nd column of an item in the following table occur in relation to the biological; and (b) the person is referred to in the 3rd column of that item. Circumstances in which requirements may be imposed Item Circumstance relating to biological Person subject to requirements It is supplied while it is included in the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied that it does not conform with a standard applicable to it The person in relation to whom it is included in the Register It is a biological, other than a Class 1 biological, and it is supplied while it is included in the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied that the manufacturing principles have not been observed in its manufacture The person in relation to whom it is included in the Register  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Public notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8 Section 32HA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Circumstances in which requirements may be imposed Item Circumstance relating to biological Person subject to requirements It is supplied while: (a) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in relation to the biological or the biological is exempt under subsection 32CA(2); or (b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or (c) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CK(1); or (d) it is the subject of an authority under subsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or (e) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2); but the Secretary is satisfied that it does not conform with a standard applicable to it The person supplying it It is a biological, other than a Class 1 biological, and it is supplied while: (a) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in relation to the biological or the biological is exempt under subsection 32CA(2); or (b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or (c) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CK(1); or (d) it is the subject of an authority under subsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or (e) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2); but the Secretary is satisfied that the manufacturing principles have not been observed in its manufacture The person supplying it 4A. It is supplied and the Secretary is satisfied that: (a) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the purposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—the supply contravenes one or more of those The person supplying it  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Secretary may, by notice in writing, impose requirements, relating to a biological, on a person if: (a) any of the circumstances referred to in the 2nd column of an item in the following table occur in relation to the biological; and (b) the person is referred to in the 3rd column of that item. Circumstances in which requirements may be imposed Item Circumstance relating to biological Person subject to requirements It is supplied while it is included in the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied that it does not conform with a standard applicable to it The person in relation to whom it is included in the Register It is a biological, other than a Class 1 biological, and it is supplied while it is included in the Register, but the Secretary is satisfied that the manufacturing principles have not been observed in its manufacture The person in relation to whom it is included in the Register  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Biologicals  Part 3-2A Public notification, and recall, of biologicals  Division 8 Section 32HA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Circumstances in which requirements may be imposed Item Circumstance relating to biological Person subject to requirements It is supplied while: (a) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in relation to the biological or the biological is exempt under subsection 32CA(2); or (b) it is exempt under section 32CB; or (c) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CK(1); or (d) it is the subject of an authority under subsection 32CM(1) or (7A); or (e) it is the subject of an approval under subsection 32CO(1), (1A) or (2); but the Secretary is satisfied that it does not conform with a standard applicable to it The person supplying it It is a biological, other than a Class 1 biological, and it is supplied while: (a) the person is exempt under subsection 32CA(1) in relation to the biological or the biological is exempt under subsection 32C"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b8704ece98d6847693b714453eb76eadcc8f17405d135858207e62dc7fca44f1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "360"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Secretary may impose requirements on a person supplying a biological if certain circumstances occur." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.360" ;
