    values:originalText "(4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person, at premises in Australia, carries out a step in the manufacture of therapeutic goods (other than goods exempt under section 18A or 32CB); and (b) the goods are for supply for use in humans; and (c) none of the following applies: (i) the goods are exempt goods; (ii) the person is an exempt person in relation to the manufacture of the goods; (iii) the person is the holder of a licence that is in force that authorises the carrying out of that step in relation to the goods at those premises. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both.  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
