doc:sec-35a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35A Civil penalties relating to manufacturing therapeutic goods" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person contravenes this subsection if: (a) the person carries out a step in the manufacture of therapeutic goods at premises in Australia; and  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "383"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35B Criminal offences relating to breaching a condition of a licence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-35b ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence; and (d) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Manufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3  Section 35C Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. (4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. (5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence. Penalty: 100 penalty units. (6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence; and (d) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person.  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices  Chapter 3 Manufacturing of therapeutic goods  Part 3-3  Section 35C Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. (4) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. (5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person holds a licence; and (b) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (c) the act or omission breaches a condition of the licence. Penalty: 100 penalty units. (6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "02313874176523de19d0d6e1d970fc312694bb1783de6dbedd474e7334f2d0eb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "384"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-35b-ss-4 ;
