concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-39 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "39 Term of licence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-39 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A licence commences on the day specified in the licence and remains in force until it is revoked or suspended. (2) If: (a) the licence covers therapeutic goods that are exempt under section 18A; and (b) those goods cease to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to those goods when those goods cease to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 18A may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the goods covered by the exemption, see subsection 18A(5). (3) If: (a) the licence covers a biological that is exempt under section 32CB; and (b) the biological ceases to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to the biological when the biological ceases to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 32CB may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the biologicals covered by the exemption: see subsections 32CB(5) and 32CD(1)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A licence commences on the day specified in the licence and remains in force until it is revoked or suspended. (2) If: (a) the licence covers therapeutic goods that are exempt under section 18A; and (b) those goods cease to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to those goods when those goods cease to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 18A may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the goods covered by the exemption, see subsection 18A(5). (3) If: (a) the licence covers a biological that is exempt under section 32CB; and (b) the biological ceases to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to the biological when the biological ceases to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 32CB may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the biologicals covered by the exemption: see subsections 32CB(5) and 32CD(1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c49f966472fae46b958b98656afa786943d9eac4d16f4e8d8fa9e8e3202d04af" ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-39-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-39-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-39-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.394" .
doc:sec-39 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "39 Term of licence" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A licence commences on the day specified in the licence and remains in force until it is revoked or suspended. (2) If: (a) the licence covers therapeutic goods that are exempt under section 18A; and (b) those goods cease to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to those goods when those goods cease to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 18A may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the goods covered by the exemption, see subsection 18A(5). (3) If: (a) the licence covers a biological that is exempt under section 32CB; and (b) the biological ceases to be exempt under that section before the licence is revoked; the licence ceases to be in force in relation to the biological when the biological ceases to be exempt under that section. Note: An exemption under section 32CB may cease to have effect only in relation to some of the biologicals covered by the exemption: see subsections 32CB(5) and 32CD(1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer .

