doc:sec-40b-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40B(3) Variation of licences—application by licence holder" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If an application is made under subsection (1) and any applicable prescribed inspection fees have been paid, the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the holder of the licence, vary the licence so that the licence covers each additional manufacturing site specified in the notice." ;
    cof:pageNumber "398"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-40b-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40B(4) Variation of licences—application by licence holder"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40b-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) For each manufacturing site specified under subsection (3), the Secretary must, in the notice under that subsection, vary the licence to authorise the holder of the licence to carry out specified steps in the manufacture of specified therapeutic goods at that manufacturing site. Note 1: For specification by class, see subsection 33(3AB) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Note 2: Section 40A and subsections (6) to (9) of this section deal with variation of authorisations." ;
    skos:definition "(4) For each manufacturing site specified under subsection (3), the Secretary must, in the notice under that subsection, vary the licence to authorise the holder of the licence to carry out specified steps in the manufacture of specified therapeutic goods at that manufacturing site. Note 1: For specification by class, see subsection 33(3AB) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Note 2: Section 40A and subsections (6) to (9) of this section deal with variation of authorisations."@en ;
