concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41 Revocation and suspension of licences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the holder of a licence, revoke the licence, or suspend the licence for a period specified in the notice, if: (a) at least one of the following persons: (i) the holder; (ii) a person (a manager) who makes, or participates in making, decisions that affect the whole, or a substantial part, of the holder’s affairs; (iii) if the holder is a body corporate—a major interest holder of the body corporate; has: (iv) been convicted of an offence against this Act or a corresponding State law; or (v) been convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (vi) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of this Act or a corresponding State law; or (vii) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (viii) breached a condition of a manufacturing licence; or (ix) had a manufacturing licence suspended or revoked; or  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the holder of a licence, revoke the licence, or suspend the licence for a period specified in the notice, if: (a) at least one of the following persons: (i) the holder; (ii) a person (a manager) who makes, or participates in making, decisions that affect the whole, or a substantial part, of the holder’s affairs; (iii) if the holder is a body corporate—a major interest holder of the body corporate; has: (iv) been convicted of an offence against this Act or a corresponding State law; or (v) been convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (vi) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of this Act or a corresponding State law; or (vii) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (viii) breached a condition of a manufacturing licence; or (ix) had a manufacturing licence suspended or revoked; or  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f6fbda13eb4b0aa914a819e81dadaddea46f623e8f2b38a0025ed1e084bef85d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "401"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Revocation or suspension of a licence for specified reasons" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.401" ;
    cml:asserts concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41-norm .
