    cof:title "41 Revocation and suspension of licences" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the holder of a licence, revoke the licence, or suspend the licence for a period specified in the notice, if: (a) at least one of the following persons: (i) the holder; (ii) a person (a manager) who makes, or participates in making, decisions that affect the whole, or a substantial part, of the holder’s affairs; (iii) if the holder is a body corporate—a major interest holder of the body corporate; has: (iv) been convicted of an offence against this Act or a corresponding State law; or (v) been convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (vi) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of this Act or a corresponding State law; or (vii) been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty for the contravention of a civil penalty provision of a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory involving fraud or dishonesty; or (viii) breached a condition of a manufacturing licence; or (ix) had a manufacturing licence suspended or revoked; or  Chapter 3  Medicines and other therapeutic goods that are not medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "401"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41AA Spent convictions scheme"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41aa ;
    values:originalText "Nothing in section 40 or 41 affects the operation of Part VIIC of the Crimes Act 1914 (which includes provisions that, in certain circumstances, relieve persons from the requirement to disclose spent convictions and require persons aware of such convictions to disregard them)." ;
    skos:definition "Nothing in section 40 or 41 affects the operation of Part VIIC of the Crimes Act 1914 (which includes provisions that, in certain circumstances, relieve persons from the requirement to disclose spent convictions and require persons aware of such convictions to disregard them)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "26a042a4750a2b1bf06d170e8a3c7ea9fa8618b617f178ccd724915efff5183c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "404"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Relieves persons from the requirement to disclose spent convictions and require persons aware of such convictions to disregard them." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.404" ;
    cml:asserts concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41aa-norm .
